        "problem": "Which of the following number lines gives the solution to $-2\\le 3x-5\\le 4?$",
        "worked_solution": "We isolate $x$ by applying the addition and multiplication principles, as usual.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\le 3x-5\\le 4 \\\\ -2+5 & \\le 3x-5+5\\le 4+5 \\\\ 3 & \\le 3x\\le 9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{3} & \\le \\frac{3x}{3}\\le \\frac{9}{3} \\\\ 1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we can represent the solution in a number line as follows  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13944026/assets/bab168cd93d52c9a36f8d5bc8e905f009b2779618643acafaa4fae7eeb28abca.png)",
